<SiteLayout title="Privacy — Sentinel Agency" description="Sentinel Agency privacy notice for recruiting and staffing interactions.">
<section class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p><h1>Recruiting data deserves deliberate handling.</h1><p class="lede">Sentinel Agency is building its recruiting platform around data minimization, consent, role-based access, auditability and separation of sensitive candidate information from public talent profiles.</p><div class="cards"><article><span>01</span><h3>Candidate data</h3><p>Contact details, work history, compensation context, work authorization, interview notes and placement records may be processed when voluntarily provided or required to run a search.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Employer data</h3><p>Role briefs, hiring contacts, interview feedback, commercial terms and staffing operations data may be processed to deliver recruiting services.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Consent & deletion</h3><p>Consent, opt-out, archival and deletion states are designed as first-class records rather than hidden flags.</p></article></div><p>This launch notice is informational and will be replaced with the agency's final legal privacy policy before collecting production PII through the website.</p></section>
</SiteLayout>
